# Hooks are executed by bash. If a Windows checkout writes CRLF into a .sh file,
# bash fails with `$'\r': command not found` — which for a failClosed hook means
# every prompt is blocked and the agent is unusable. Force LF on everything
# executable, and normalise text generally.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mdc text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply text/EOL normalisation.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
